The distance Tom travels out is $10 \text{ mph} \times 3 \text{ hours} = 30 \text{ miles}$.
To travel back 30 miles at 6 mph, it takes $30 / 6 = 5$ hours.

\boxed{5}

The total time required is 180 minutes (3 hours). To have the cake ready by 5:00 pm, Jordan needs to start 3 hours earlier.

5:00 pm minus 3 hours is 2:00 pm.

\boxed{2:00 \text{ pm}}

Bernice has driven $325 \times 4 = 1300$ kilometers.
The remaining distance is $1955 - 1300 = 655$ kilometers.

\boxed{655}
